// Design D18 (activity sense): about an hour and three quarters of someone's afternoon, in virtual time (Replay Items,
// at_ms after launch; `front_name` is the front app's display name, taken out by the driver and never logged or kept).
// 14:00 Tue, quiet hours 22:30-07:30 (default). Expected check-ins (crates/buddy-app/src/unprompted.rs
// `activity_sense_fixture_...`, driven through `Unprompted::sample`): long_dwell at 45 min (VS Code), flip_loop at
// 64 min (the 6th app switch of 6 in 4 min 10 s: VS Code/Chrome/Slack), ONE back_from_idle at 87 min, enriched with the app before the break (never a
// second turn for the same return), and, only with quiet hours turned off, one late_hour at 100 min (the clock jumps
// to 23:10). With activity off the same lines give the plain back_from_idle and nothing else.
// Live: `BUDDY_EVENTS=<this file> cargo run -p buddy-app` (sensors are off under it) plays it in real time (~103 min). In a debug
// build BUDDY_ACTIVITY_SCALE=<n> divides the activity thresholds (long_dwell, flip window, back_after_away) by n, for a
// copy of this file with the at_ms of the app lines divided by n; BUDDY_SENSES_LOG=1 prints `[buddy] activity <kind>`.
